      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brownton began as Grimshaw Settlement and was officially founded in 1877 by Alonzo Brown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.twincities.com/2020/05/10/more-to-the-story-the-origins-of-brownton-and-lake-addie/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Alonzo Brown named the town after his brother Charles, who died in the Civil War siege of Cornith, Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.twincities.com/2020/05/10/more-to-the-story-the-origins-of-brownton-and-lake-addie/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad transformed Brownton, turning it into a thriving mid‑century community before recent decline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.twincities.com/2020/05/10/more-to-the-story-the-origins-of-brownton-and-lake-addie/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office has served Brownton continuously since 1878, marking its early civic infrastructure.",
